WEBVTT

00:01.620 --> 00:03.570
Sorry for showing up at this hour.

00:04.230 --> 00:06.330
It's okay. We don't mind.

00:06.330 --> 00:08.190
What is it? Something important?

00:08.190 --> 00:11.240
Do you remember Cardinal Ljubo?

00:11.240 --> 00:15.240
Yeah. I saw him at the 
Great Last Wall Fortress.

00:16.170 --> 00:20.030
He's looking for the former 
demon lord's airship.

00:35.220 --> 00:41.930
<b>Banished from the Hero's Party,
I Decided to Live a Quiet Life in the Countryside 2nd</b>

01:52.500 --> 01:56.510
<b>The Man Who Doesn't Get Chill Living</b>

01:55.450 --> 01:58.280
"Masked Knight Escarlata"

01:58.280 --> 02:01.240
"defeats Altra of the Water, 
general of the demon lord's army,"

02:01.240 --> 02:02.970
"and forces Altra into retreat."

02:03.190 --> 02:05.670
I wonder who she serves.

02:05.670 --> 02:07.760
The Church? Or...

02:07.760 --> 02:09.340
It seems she's a mercenary.

02:09.340 --> 02:10.230
Oh.

02:11.470 --> 02:16.660
You know, the former demon lord's 
airship, which Tisse brought up...

02:17.170 --> 02:19.740
Are you sure you want to 
hand it over to the Church?

02:20.060 --> 02:24.240
I think they'll put it to much better 
use than letting it rot away in Zoltan.

02:24.840 --> 02:27.540
If they want to misuse it, 
we should stop them,

02:28.000 --> 02:29.790
but for the time being, 
we'll wait and see.

02:29.790 --> 02:31.040
Okay.

02:31.040 --> 02:35.540
Our top priority right now is 
making sure nobody finds Ruti.

02:37.590 --> 02:39.880
Looks like the cold mold's gone.

02:43.590 --> 02:46.220
The herbs are growing nicely, too.

02:46.220 --> 02:47.500
Yeah.

02:47.500 --> 02:50.230
It's thanks to your advice, Big Brother.

02:50.230 --> 02:53.690
And also because Tisse was with me.

02:53.690 --> 02:58.490
Right. I'm having a lot of fun growing 
this farm with Miss Ruti, too.

02:58.770 --> 03:02.380
We'll have to think of a sales plan soon.

03:02.380 --> 03:04.790
Let's start with my apothecary.

03:04.790 --> 03:06.940
I'll buy your first harvest.

03:06.940 --> 03:07.750
Okay.

03:07.750 --> 03:11.300
We should try talking to the 
Merchants' Guild, Zoltan's clinics,

03:12.050 --> 03:14.960
and also traveling merchants.

03:15.440 --> 03:17.990
You'll help us out?

03:17.990 --> 03:21.770
Yeah. I'm a member of the Merchants' Guild,

03:21.770 --> 03:24.970
and your mentor in Zoltan chill living.

03:25.770 --> 03:27.600
Master Big Brother!

03:28.310 --> 03:30.290
Master Big Brother...

03:30.290 --> 03:31.150
Hm?

03:33.070 --> 03:35.480
A lovely phrase.

03:54.050 --> 03:56.000
You look in good shape.

03:56.000 --> 03:57.130
Good enough.

03:57.560 --> 04:01.000
The rest I'll regain through combat.

04:01.000 --> 04:03.840
You're going to leave Zoltan 
once you're discharged?

04:03.840 --> 04:05.140
I'll miss you.

04:05.140 --> 04:07.150
Then come with me.

04:07.150 --> 04:09.890
Let's go massacre the demon lord's army!

04:09.890 --> 04:14.100
Nah. I've decided to live here 
and run my apothecary with Rit.

04:14.290 --> 04:16.610
That so? Too bad.

04:16.610 --> 04:19.570
Let's go get a drink while you're still here.

04:19.570 --> 04:24.300
Sure. But there's something I need 
to do before I bid you goodbye.

04:24.300 --> 04:25.030
What?

04:26.190 --> 04:27.230
Gideon.

04:29.190 --> 04:31.340
Spar with me.

04:33.770 --> 04:36.040
And you accepted?

04:36.040 --> 04:37.380
Yeah.

04:37.380 --> 04:40.580
He insisted he wanted to 
before leaving Zoltan.

04:41.070 --> 04:44.550
I'll have to train like crazy. 
I've probably lost my edge by now.

04:44.550 --> 04:46.120
Can you win?

04:46.120 --> 04:48.190
Honestly, not a chance.

04:48.640 --> 04:50.980
Danan's Blessing is Martial Artist.

04:50.980 --> 04:52.660
It's a common Blessing,

04:52.660 --> 04:56.420
but nobody out there has loved their Blessing, 
and been loved by it in turn, as much as him.

04:56.420 --> 04:57.520
Oh...

04:57.520 --> 04:59.690
Meanwhile, I'm the Guide.

05:00.180 --> 05:03.460
I only have common skills 
meant to protect a young Hero.

05:04.020 --> 05:06.820
It's obvious how this will go.

05:07.140 --> 05:08.820
But you're still going to spar?

05:09.800 --> 05:10.830
Yeah.

05:11.100 --> 05:12.310
Huh...

05:12.790 --> 05:14.830
In that case, could you spar with me, too?

05:17.920 --> 05:23.760
What's with the look...

05:18.130 --> 05:21.820
I mean, we haven't ever sparred before.

05:21.820 --> 05:24.790
It'll be fine if you cast Merciful.

05:24.790 --> 05:27.530
I bet you're gonna use it against Danan, too.

05:28.070 --> 05:33.860
Well, sure, if I cast the spell, 
I won't scar or injure my opponent.

05:34.110 --> 05:36.380
But it'll still hurt.

05:41.350 --> 05:42.440
I can't!

05:42.400 --> 05:44.320
<b>Gah</b>

05:50.320 --> 05:51.910
<i>I'm so rusty.</i>

05:52.460 --> 05:55.500
<i>I'll end up disappointing Danan this way.</i>

05:55.690 --> 05:58.720
Here, be sure to hydrate.

05:58.720 --> 06:00.020
Thanks.

06:00.020 --> 06:02.090
Red!

06:02.500 --> 06:05.460
I hear you're fighting Danan!

06:05.910 --> 06:07.740
Word gets around, huh?

06:08.180 --> 06:11.010
That means I'm perfect for the job.

06:11.470 --> 06:15.220
Train with me to regain 
your combat instincts!

06:15.490 --> 06:19.480
But aren't you a spirit mage?

06:20.730 --> 06:24.980
Believe it or not, I'm the founder 
of the Lotus-Style Staff Technique.

06:24.980 --> 06:28.700
What?! That style's famous everywhere!

06:24.980 --> 06:33.830
<b>Lotus-Style
Staff
Technique</b>

06:28.700 --> 06:30.780
That's not all.

06:30.780 --> 06:34.750
You know that book detailing 
various regions' military tactics?

06:34.030 --> 06:41.000
<b>100 Strategies:
The Beauty of War
Compiled by Yarandrala</b>

06:34.750 --> 06:36.850
The famous <i>100 Strategies: 
The Beauty of War</i>?

06:36.850 --> 06:39.480
She compiled that, too.

06:39.480 --> 06:41.000
Whoa!

06:41.350 --> 06:44.170
I'm not just living out 
my years doing nothing.

06:45.480 --> 06:47.630
So, back to the topic at hand...

06:48.010 --> 06:52.790
What you need right now, Red, 
is to sharpen your mind.

06:52.790 --> 06:56.220
It's not easy to regain your past skills.

06:56.220 --> 07:00.480
But your mind must possess a different 
kind of strength than it did in the past!

07:00.700 --> 07:04.980
True. I've gained a lot 
since I moved to Zoltan.

07:05.440 --> 07:09.490
Then I guess I'll train in a way 
that plays to <i>Red's</i> strengths.

07:09.710 --> 07:11.060
That's the spirit!

07:11.060 --> 07:13.800
Then let's get right to 
planning the training camp.

07:13.800 --> 07:14.920
Training camp?

07:14.920 --> 07:16.870
You're coming too, of course.

07:21.830 --> 07:23.410
Did you wait long, Big Brother?

07:23.410 --> 07:25.880
Nah, I just got here.

07:27.200 --> 07:30.870
You just wanted to play 
that scene out, didn't you?

07:31.180 --> 07:33.890
"Did you wait long?" "No, I just got here."

07:33.890 --> 07:37.640
Is that so? It's adorable how 
much she cares for her brother.

07:37.640 --> 07:39.410
Did you wait long, Big Brother?

07:39.410 --> 07:41.200
Nah, I just got here.

07:41.200 --> 07:42.700
Did you want long, Big Brother?!

07:42.700 --> 07:44.580
Nah? I just got here.

07:44.580 --> 07:45.690
Big Brother, did you—

07:45.690 --> 07:50.150
Anyway, are you sure you can 
handle training with Miss Ruti?

07:50.150 --> 07:53.100
I'm the one who taught 
her the sword, you know?

07:53.100 --> 07:56.040
There's no way a teacher and 
student can't train together.

07:56.040 --> 07:59.200
I'm really looking forward 
to training with you.

07:59.530 --> 08:02.570
A training camp is a method to grow stronger,

08:02.570 --> 08:04.280
and it's also the ultimate 
form of recreation.

08:05.400 --> 08:07.980
Danan! Were you discharged?

08:07.980 --> 08:11.760
Yeah. And you know just how 
much I love training camps.

08:12.110 --> 08:14.260
So I'm joining ya!

08:14.500 --> 08:17.720
That's so you. Sure, join us.

08:18.070 --> 08:19.070
Yeah!

08:26.040 --> 08:28.670
All right. That just leaves firewood...

08:28.670 --> 08:29.760
Hey...

08:39.740 --> 08:42.750
Hey! Don't go around 
destroying the ecosystem!

08:44.240 --> 08:47.250
All right! I'm going on another firewood run!

08:47.250 --> 08:48.760
Yeah, that's all wrong.

08:49.880 --> 08:53.820
The first meal of training camp 
is Red's custom training lunch!

08:57.010 --> 09:01.010
Oh, right. I don't think 
we have any for you, Danan.

09:01.170 --> 09:02.600
You can have mine.

09:02.600 --> 09:04.830
I couldn't!

09:06.060 --> 09:11.020
Don't worry. The pangs of hunger 
are also a new experience for me.

09:11.420 --> 09:13.780
Let's go halfsies, Miss Ruti.

09:13.780 --> 09:16.410
You can have half of mine, too.

09:20.910 --> 09:23.280
Half and half makes one whole.

09:23.800 --> 09:25.680
That doesn't seem right.

09:26.220 --> 09:28.420
Wait, wait. Let's try this instead.

09:29.260 --> 09:31.320
Now we all grab whatever we want.

09:31.320 --> 09:32.920
That's my Big Brother!

09:33.180 --> 09:34.700
My bad.

09:34.700 --> 09:38.300
But since you're offering, 
I'll happily indulge!

09:45.250 --> 09:46.500
Say something, dude.

09:50.870 --> 09:54.710
It's been a long time since the 
Hero's party got together like this.

09:54.710 --> 09:57.700
We're missing Theodora... and Ares, though.

10:01.160 --> 10:02.390
True that.

10:04.120 --> 10:06.050
Did you see the newspaper?

10:06.050 --> 10:11.460
The news about that mystery mercenary 
who fought off Astra of the Water?

10:11.760 --> 10:14.460
You mean the Masked Knight Escarlata?

10:14.690 --> 10:16.850
That's gotta be Theodora.

10:16.850 --> 10:21.440
There ain't another knight on this 
continent who can best a general.

10:21.920 --> 10:26.070
And then there's Escarlata's right-hand man,

10:26.070 --> 10:28.060
the knight with a prosthetic right arm.

10:28.700 --> 10:30.860
That must be Albert.

10:31.230 --> 10:35.230
Oh, him? I haven't thanked 
him for saving me yet.

10:35.500 --> 10:39.630
I'm planning to meet up with Theodora 
first thing after leaving Zoltan.

10:39.630 --> 10:42.610
If she wants to go finish 
off the Water General,

10:42.610 --> 10:44.740
then I'll happily join her.

10:45.990 --> 10:49.910
I still haven't tried the 
duck sauté, you know.

10:49.910 --> 10:51.250
Like I care.

10:51.500 --> 10:53.360
Hey, stop that!

10:52.630 --> 10:54.040
Why, you...

10:54.980 --> 10:56.160
Yubby.

10:56.160 --> 10:57.800
Ruti!

11:00.070 --> 11:01.890
Okay, let's get to it!

11:06.720 --> 11:08.290
Should we get train, too?

11:08.290 --> 11:09.190
Sounds good.

11:09.190 --> 11:11.470
There's something else I want to do.

11:11.780 --> 11:13.110
Miss Ruti?

11:58.950 --> 12:03.290
That was, like... kind of 
not what I was expecting.

12:03.290 --> 12:06.880
Really? It was exactly what I expected.

12:07.520 --> 12:08.540
Right.

12:08.540 --> 12:11.040
What were you imagining?

12:12.920 --> 12:14.580
Something smells nice.

12:14.580 --> 12:19.080
I heard Rit and Yarandrala 
are making dinner tonight.

12:19.510 --> 12:20.660
This should be good.

12:24.930 --> 12:27.410
Your swordplay makes your foe visible.

12:27.410 --> 12:28.510
My foe?

12:28.720 --> 12:32.770
Yeah. I can see exactly who you're
 cutting down with your moves.

12:33.960 --> 12:36.220
Yeah, well, I'm picturing them in my mind.

12:37.110 --> 12:40.590
People, elves, monsters, demons.

12:40.910 --> 12:44.670
I can clearly see a different 
foe of yours each time.

12:45.030 --> 12:48.120
That shows how adaptable your tactics are.

12:48.120 --> 12:50.290
Sparring with you will be fun!

12:50.850 --> 12:51.940
Likewise.

13:06.980 --> 13:09.330
Shall I wash your back?

13:15.910 --> 13:18.230
I'll take you up on that.

13:25.060 --> 13:29.610
Training with him today really
 drove home how strong Danan is.

13:29.610 --> 13:33.840
I think he's the strongest human 
out here except for Ruti.

13:33.840 --> 13:36.750
Yeah, I felt the same.

13:37.050 --> 13:41.030
But sparring with him is neither 
a sport nor a fight to the death.

13:41.360 --> 13:44.210
It has an objective outside 
of winning and losing.

13:44.210 --> 13:45.760
And what's that?

13:46.030 --> 13:48.160
Danan's a warrior to the core.

13:48.160 --> 13:50.320
The farthest thing from a chill life.

13:50.820 --> 13:55.090
Through our battles, I want to show 
him how I've chosen to live my life.

13:55.770 --> 13:58.040
He's a friend who you've been 
on adventures with, after all.

13:58.460 --> 13:59.940
I hope he understands.

14:01.240 --> 14:02.130
Yeah.

14:10.840 --> 14:13.950
Okay, I'm casting Merciful.

14:16.680 --> 14:20.660
You won't get injured, but know that 
this spell doesn't dampen pain.

14:25.380 --> 14:27.380
No hard feelings.

14:29.630 --> 14:30.890
Begin!

14:35.930 --> 14:36.890
Martial Art:

14:36.890 --> 14:38.060
Rampaging Kick!

14:59.580 --> 15:01.570
Martial Art: Pulverizing Punch!

15:10.200 --> 15:12.940
It really is just a normal sword.

15:12.940 --> 15:15.760
I'm supposed to be far stronger than you,

15:15.760 --> 15:20.530
but you saw through all my moves and even 
made contact with me using your sword.

15:23.530 --> 15:26.200
You're fun, Gideon.

15:26.200 --> 15:28.360
You really are fun.

15:28.360 --> 15:31.860
You've figured out how to win, 
though, haven't you?

15:31.860 --> 15:36.310
Yeah. You're only dealing with my attacks

15:36.310 --> 15:39.790
because you're predicting them.

15:40.370 --> 15:43.880
There's no way I'd be able 
to defend myself otherwise.

15:44.050 --> 15:47.810
In that case, I can simply win with 
moves I wouldn't normally use.

15:47.810 --> 15:50.380
Holding back a little is all it'll take.

15:50.380 --> 15:53.890
I guess. Well? Are you going to hold back?

15:54.320 --> 15:56.270
Hell no.

15:56.270 --> 15:58.840
This is a sparring match,
 not a battle to the death.

15:59.300 --> 16:04.740
I'm gonna fight you at my absolute peak!

16:04.740 --> 16:06.520
I expected nothing else!

16:07.700 --> 16:09.480
Here I come, Gideon.

16:09.730 --> 16:13.520
If you're seeing through me at full strength,

16:13.520 --> 16:17.150
I'll just show you I can go beyond!

16:17.530 --> 16:18.780
Bring it, Danan.

16:19.190 --> 16:23.290
I'll match you using everything 
I've gained in my life so far!

16:28.460 --> 16:29.680
Gideon!

16:30.340 --> 16:31.510
Danan!

16:38.500 --> 16:42.480
Ow... I should've known
 I couldn't handle a direct hit.

16:43.550 --> 16:46.480
I'd be a goner if it weren't 
for Yarandrala's spell.

16:48.410 --> 16:51.240
You really are strong, Gideon.

16:51.240 --> 16:53.640
I hope I didn't disappoint you.

16:53.640 --> 16:54.950
Of course not.

16:55.480 --> 16:58.170
I don't get this chill life business.

16:58.650 --> 17:01.780
That's exactly why I wanted to spar with you.

17:02.070 --> 17:04.960
Fighting's the only thing I'm good for.

17:04.960 --> 17:08.210
So, did you understand anything 
about the chill life?

17:08.440 --> 17:10.010
Not a thing.

17:10.010 --> 17:13.330
But, Gideon... No, Red.

17:13.330 --> 17:17.300
I saw that your swordplay has an 
underlying, unrelenting strength.

17:17.850 --> 17:20.920
You are still that strong man 
I've come to respect.

17:20.920 --> 17:22.470
You just chose another path.

17:22.860 --> 17:25.600
This chill living thing could 
be a different form of strength.

17:26.050 --> 17:28.230
Do your damnedest to live happily ever after.

17:28.230 --> 17:30.290
Thank you, Danan.

17:30.290 --> 17:33.540
I fight because I constantly desire battle.

17:33.540 --> 17:35.740
That's my source of pride.

17:35.740 --> 17:41.240
Right. I respect your 
relentless strength, too.

17:43.200 --> 17:46.190
Danan. My turn next.

17:46.960 --> 17:50.750
What? I can spar with the strongest Hero?!

17:50.750 --> 17:52.920
Not even in my wildest dreams...

17:55.920 --> 18:00.390
Darn it! How can I win?

18:03.940 --> 18:06.020
I feel so bad for him.

18:06.020 --> 18:07.020
Sorry.

18:15.930 --> 18:17.900
If it isn't Albert!

18:17.900 --> 18:19.580
It's been a while.

18:19.580 --> 18:22.910
Talk about a surprise. 
You're back in Zoltan?

18:22.910 --> 18:25.030
I just got here today.

18:25.030 --> 18:28.160
I'm glad to see you well, 
Mister Red, Miss Rit.

18:28.160 --> 18:30.920
"Mister" Red? That feels weird.

18:32.260 --> 18:35.420
Please don't bring up who I used to be.

18:35.640 --> 18:37.420
Is Theodora with you?

18:37.420 --> 18:39.740
I came alone.

18:39.740 --> 18:43.280
She's currently going by 
the name of Escarlata.

18:43.280 --> 18:46.680
And I bring you a message from her.

18:46.680 --> 18:47.930
A message?

18:48.970 --> 18:51.450
"A new Hero has appeared."

18:52.120 --> 18:54.690
"He is Van of Flamberge."

18:55.360 --> 19:00.700
"He may make his way to Zoltan in order to
 take the former demon lord's airship."

19:08.270 --> 19:09.940
What a ruckus.

19:09.940 --> 19:11.540
Everyone's having fun.

19:13.540 --> 19:16.730
Stay close, Lavender. It's not safe.

19:16.730 --> 19:19.340
But you'll protect me, won't you?

19:19.340 --> 19:22.050
Of course. I'll keep you 
safe with all I have.

19:22.050 --> 19:26.560
Gosh! I could do anything for you, Van!

19:28.260 --> 19:31.100
What have you been grinning at?!

19:31.100 --> 19:34.560
W-Well, this is self-defense now.

19:37.050 --> 19:43.960
I-I... I gotta kill people every now and 
then to keep my Blessing in control!

19:45.490 --> 19:48.580
Any of his friends around?

19:48.580 --> 19:52.870
Why don't you attack me to avenge him?!

19:52.870 --> 19:55.500
Come on! Come at me!

19:55.500 --> 19:58.670
I-I beg of you! Give me your life!

19:55.880 --> 19:57.390
A Wrongdoer Blessing, huh?

20:07.090 --> 20:08.370
The evil is gone.

20:13.510 --> 20:15.520
What happened here?

20:15.520 --> 20:18.390
Van just struck down a strange fellow.

20:18.390 --> 20:22.780
Right. I killed him because 
he murdered someone.

20:23.140 --> 20:26.950
I need a full explanation. 
Why did the fight break out?

20:26.950 --> 20:30.340
Huh? Is that important?

20:30.340 --> 20:33.290
It is important to know 
what motivated the killing.

20:33.690 --> 20:37.290
You could have easily captured him alive.

20:37.740 --> 20:40.300
You should have interrogated him first.

20:40.550 --> 20:45.540
Why should I? You do realize he had
 a Wrongdoer Blessing, I assume?

20:46.030 --> 20:48.160
But everyone here is human.

20:48.480 --> 20:51.400
People's lives involve more than 
their Blessings' urges alone.

20:51.890 --> 20:54.160
Every person has their own free will.

20:54.160 --> 20:55.810
You must never forget that.

20:56.510 --> 20:58.840
You're mistaken.

20:58.840 --> 20:59.780
What?

20:59.780 --> 21:04.280
Oh, no, I don't mean to imply 
that what you're saying is wrong.

21:05.130 --> 21:10.730
I did not hate him, nor was I trying 
to stop any further killings.

21:11.130 --> 21:14.580
Using the Hero's blade to satisfy 
personal desires is wrong.

21:14.580 --> 21:18.580
Not to mention, my battles are all 
offerings to the Almighty Demis.

21:18.580 --> 21:20.590
Why, then, did you kill him?

21:20.930 --> 21:25.810
People with Wrongdoer exist to 
be taken down by someone else.

21:25.810 --> 21:29.840
I killed him so he could fulfill his role.

21:30.100 --> 21:35.410
And I certainly did feel I grew 
as Hero when I killed him.

21:36.460 --> 21:39.280
I offer love and blessings to his life.

21:39.840 --> 21:42.820
My Blessing, which has now 
grown at the cost of his life,

21:42.820 --> 21:44.860
will surely save the world one day.

21:44.860 --> 21:46.850
Van, why are you so...

21:46.850 --> 21:48.870
The words of a true Hero indeed.

21:49.160 --> 21:51.930
Please. I'm still a Hero in name only.

21:51.930 --> 21:55.250
I haven't even fought the demon lord's army.

21:55.680 --> 22:00.260
Surely Hero Ruti's faith must 
run far deeper than mine.

22:04.900 --> 22:07.470
Come. We head to Zoltan.
